course: dictionary
lesson: 13437
title: Horizontally: flat, side to side
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Horizontally means in a flat, level direction, from side to side. It comes from horizon, the flat line where the sky meets the land or sea. Something that lies horizontally lies flat, like a line lying down.
explain: Use the words around it to check. «Lay the ruler horizontally across the page.» Across the page is side to side, so horizontally must mean flat, from side to side. The sentence gives you the clue.
explain: Swap in your meaning to test it: «Lay the ruler flat, from side to side across the page.» It still makes sense, so you have it right. Vertically is the opposite: that means up and down, like a tree standing tall.
fact: Horizontally means in a flat, level direction, from side to side.
fact: Horizontally is an adverb: it tells you how something lies, moves or is drawn.
fact: The opposite of horizontally is vertically, which means up and down.
fact: On a graph, the x-axis runs horizontally, from left to right.
fact: In a table, the rows run horizontally and the columns run vertically.
exercise: «Lay the ruler horizontally across the page.» How should the ruler lie? | Standing up tall, like a tree | *Flat, from side to side | Tilted at a steep slant
exercise: In a table, which way do the rows run? | *Side to side, horizontally | Round in a circle | Up and down | Diagonally, corner to corner
exercise: «Draw a line horizontally from the top of the box.» Find and copy the word that shows the direction. | top | *horizontally | box | line
test: «The water in the level tube lies horizontally.» What does horizontally mean here? | *Flat and level, side to side | Bubbling and hot | Standing straight up | Moving very fast
test: Which way does the x-axis on a graph run? | Diagonally | Up and down | *Horizontally, from left to right | In a circle
exam: «Fold the paper horizontally, bringing the top edge down to the bottom.» Where does the crease run? | Up and down | Round the edges | *Side to side | Diagonally across the corners
